---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base title="About Howloop" description="Who publishes Howloop, what our Australian money tools do, and the limits of our sources, AI assistance and financial review.">
 <div class="hl-wrap hl-prose-wrap"><article class="hl-prose">
  <h1>About Howloop</h1>
  <p>Howloop is an independent Australian money education project. We make everyday questions easier to work through: what lands in your bank account, how regular savings add up, and whether your next payday arrives before a bill.</p>
  <h2 id="publisher">About the publisher</h2>
  <p>Howloop publishes these tools and guides under the Howloop name. This is a small independent project, not a bank, government agency or financial-advice firm. The publisher does not claim financial-adviser or tax-agent registration. No licensed financial adviser has reviewed these guides or calculators.</p>
  <p>AI assists with drafting, translation and development. AI assistance does not establish accuracy. Each maintained guide links its sources and separates its publication, edit and source-check dates. Translations may contain errors; use the linked primary sources when a rule affects a decision.</p>
  <h2>What you can do here</h2>
  <ul><li><a href="/calculators/salary/">Estimate regular take-home pay</a> with employer super shown separately.</li><li><a href="/calculators/compound-interest/">Model savings</a> and separate your deposits from interest.</li><li><a href="/tools/cash-flow/">Plan 13 weeks of paydays and bills</a> and see the lowest projected balance.</li><li><a href="/tools/">Explore the other tools</a> for home loans, deposits, emergency funds and tax-return preparation.</li></ul>
  <h2>How to judge our numbers</h2>
  <p>Our examples are educational scenarios. They are not forecasts or recommendations to buy a product. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> explains the models and their limits. Bank data comes from dated public Consumer Data Right product feeds. Missing, old or ambiguous information must not be treated as a current offer; always check with the provider.</p>
  <p>We do not accept commissions or payment to rank bank products. Ad serving is currently disabled in this release. Any future advertising must be labelled and described in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
  <p>Report an unexpected result, confusing explanation or accessibility problem at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Please use sample amounts and leave out account numbers, TFNs and other private identifiers. Material corrections appear on <a href="/updates/">Updates</a>. See our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for what a review date means.</p>
 </article></div>
</Base>
